# Docker build-context exclusions (phase-1 task-05).
#
# Both infra/Dockerfile.api and infra/Dockerfile.web build with the REPO
# ROOT as context (`build: {context: .., dockerfile: infra/Dockerfile.*}`
# in infra/docker-compose.yml) — without this file, every `docker build`
# would tar up the multi-gigabyte reference_project/ vendor tree, every
# node_modules/.venv, and language caches before the daemon even starts
# resolving layers. None of these are COPYed by either Dockerfile, so
# excluding them changes build context size only, not image contents.

# vendored reference project — never part of any image
reference_project/

# VCS / editor / local tool state
.git/
.claude/
.superpowers/

# node / pnpm
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.next/
**/.next/

# python
.venv/
**/.venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
.import_linter_cache/
**/.import_linter_cache/

# coverage / build artifacts
coverage/
**/coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# secrets — never sent to the build daemon in the first place
.env
*.env
!.env.example

# docs — not needed inside any image
docs/
*.md
